WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.467
-Welcome back to the show. -Yeah!

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:04.567
-Yes! Exactly right! Come on.

00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:06.033
You've been on the show many times.

00:00:06.033 --> 00:00:08.000
-I have. -We love you and your sisters.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.601
But this is your first time as a guest on the couch.

00:00:10.601 --> 00:00:13.934
-I am incredibly nervous. -Are you really?

00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:16.300
-You know, I never really talk about things.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:17.601
I usually just sing. -Yeah.

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:19.968
-So I'm very -- My heart is pounding.

00:00:19.968 --> 00:00:21.167
I have to be honest.

00:00:21.167 --> 00:00:23.968
You guys are being very nice, so thank you.

00:00:23.968 --> 00:00:25.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:25.701 --> 00:00:27.601
-It is also right now after midnight,

00:00:27.601 --> 00:00:29.901
which means it's officially your birthday.

00:00:29.901 --> 00:00:31.601
So happy birthday!

00:00:31.601 --> 00:00:33.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:37.033
Come on! Come on, now. What a night this is right here.

00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:38.300
Come on.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:40.367
♪♪

00:00:40.367 --> 00:00:42.567
♪ Da, da-da, da-da ♪

00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:49.200
♪♪

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:50.367
Why you make me do the --

00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:53.567
I love -- I did the hora. I love you. Come on.

00:00:53.567 --> 00:00:55.334
-We have to do the hora. -I had to do the hora.

00:00:55.334 --> 00:00:57.067
-We had to do the hora. -Happy birthday.

00:00:57.067 --> 00:00:58.467
What birthday is it for you?

00:00:58.467 --> 00:01:01.667
-This is my dirty 30. -Oh, it's a 30th.

00:01:01.667 --> 00:01:03.834
-I am 30 years old. -Man, what a great year.

00:01:03.834 --> 00:01:06.400
I got to say. I know you just announced this giant tour.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:07.901
Haim's going on tour.

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:09.400
Thank goodness, because, man, if you want to see

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:12.200
a great live band, watch Haim.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.234
You won't even believe how fun you guys are

00:01:14.234 --> 00:01:15.634
and how talented you are.

00:01:15.634 --> 00:01:18.701
But the name -- I also love your sense of humor.

00:01:18.701 --> 00:01:21.334
The name of the tour is "One More Haim."

00:01:21.334 --> 00:01:23.501
-Yes. -♪ One More Haim ♪

00:01:23.501 --> 00:01:25.133
-Yes! You got it!

00:01:25.133 --> 00:01:26.567
-♪ And we gonna celebrate ♪ Yeah.

00:01:26.567 --> 00:01:27.801
-♪ Celebrate and dance so free ♪

00:01:27.801 --> 00:01:29.000
-"One More Haim" tour.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:30.868
Go to haimtheband.com.

00:01:30.868 --> 00:01:33.000
But you're playing Madison Square Garden, buddy.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.167
-Can you believe?

00:01:34.167 --> 00:01:35.834
-No, I can believe it. -I can't believe it.

00:01:35.834 --> 00:01:38.868
-May 17th at Madison Square Garden here in New York City.

00:01:38.868 --> 00:01:40.100
That is huge.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.734
-It's the craziest sentence of all time,

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.167
that I'm playing Madison Square Garden.

00:01:43.167 --> 00:01:45.167
We're also playing the Hollywood Bowl in L.A.,

00:01:45.167 --> 00:01:48.133
which is very wild.

00:01:48.133 --> 00:01:49.400
I'm just so excited.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:51.734
-Isn't this fun? -It's so fun. Come on.

00:01:51.734 --> 00:01:53.901
-Yeah. Can we talk about "Licorice Pizza"?

00:01:53.901 --> 00:01:57.200
Let's get into that. This is your film debut.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:58.868
Did you know that you could do this?

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:01.167
I mean, you're fantastic. -Oh, thank you.

00:02:01.167 --> 00:02:03.701
No. I did not know that I could do this.

00:02:03.701 --> 00:02:05.434
-You did not. -That is the short answer.

00:02:05.434 --> 00:02:08.200
No. I had no idea.

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:10.801
And I honestly thought that I was going to get fired every day

00:02:10.801 --> 00:02:12.467
because I had no idea what I was doing.

00:02:12.467 --> 00:02:13.834
But luckily I made it.

00:02:13.834 --> 00:02:15.667
You know, I made it to the last day of shooting.

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:17.801
And I remember turning to Paul and saying, "Am I fired?"

00:02:17.801 --> 00:02:20.534
And he'd be like, "You have asked me this every day."

00:02:20.534 --> 00:02:22.067
-I know. "You're not only -- "

00:02:22.067 --> 00:02:24.367
-"You're not fired. You're not fired."

00:02:24.367 --> 00:02:27.000
-And Paul Thomas Anderson wrote this for you.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:28.434
-Isn't that crazy? -Yeah.

00:02:28.434 --> 00:02:30.534
-I feel like I keep saying that tonight.

00:02:30.534 --> 00:02:31.968
Yes, it's crazy.

00:02:31.968 --> 00:02:34.200
-But, I mean -- You knocked it out of the park.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:35.634
I don't know if you read reviews.

00:02:35.634 --> 00:02:37.334
Do you read reviews? -I don't.

00:02:37.334 --> 00:02:38.667
I'm too nervous. -Good.

00:02:38.667 --> 00:02:41.367
-I let my mom give me, like, a daily debrief.

00:02:41.367 --> 00:02:43.667
And it's either a thumbs up or a thumbs down.

00:02:43.667 --> 00:02:46.133
-Well, this is a double thumbs up.

00:02:46.133 --> 00:02:47.734
Hopefully, Mom gave the double thumbs up.

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:48.901
Let me just say a couple things.

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:50.834
You can plug your ears if you want to.

00:02:50.834 --> 00:02:52.834
"Alana Haim makes one of the most exciting

00:02:52.834 --> 00:02:54.767
screen debuts in recent memory."

00:02:54.767 --> 00:02:56.801
From David Rooney, "The Hollywood Reporter."

00:02:56.801 --> 00:02:58.133
That's unbelievable.

00:02:58.133 --> 00:03:01.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:04.334
Peter Travers -- legend -- calls Alana's debut performance

00:03:04.334 --> 00:03:05.934
"one for the ages."

00:03:05.934 --> 00:03:07.534
Peter Travers!

00:03:07.534 --> 00:03:09.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:09.334 --> 00:03:10.801
"Variety" included "Licorice Pizza"

00:03:10.801 --> 00:03:13.400
in its list of best films of 2021.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:14.968
Look at what you did. -Oh, my goodness.

00:03:14.968 --> 00:03:18.534
-Unbelievable. Look at what you did. It's great.

00:03:18.534 --> 00:03:20.501
There's one scene with Bradley Cooper where you're --

00:03:20.501 --> 00:03:22.701
you drive him around in a delivery truck.

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:25.267
Was that you driving? -That was me driving.

00:03:25.267 --> 00:03:26.901
-Yeah. -I had to go to truck school

00:03:26.901 --> 00:03:31.167
and learn how to drive a stick shift moving van from the '70s.

00:03:31.167 --> 00:03:33.334
-Yeah. -And I'm a terrible driver.

00:03:33.334 --> 00:03:34.834
I'm terrible.

00:03:34.834 --> 00:03:37.033
And I can hear my sisters -- I'm not going to look this way

00:03:37.033 --> 00:03:40.300
because I can hear her laughing 'cause she knows.

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:41.801
I'm a terrible driver.

00:03:41.801 --> 00:03:44.667
And I didn't tell anybody that I was a bad driver.

00:03:44.667 --> 00:03:48.200
And then it came the day that I had to, you know, do it.

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:49.901
-Yeah.

00:03:49.901 --> 00:03:52.601
-I had to drive this truck, and I had Bradley Cooper.

00:03:52.601 --> 00:03:54.033
-America's sweetheart.

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:55.501
-America's sweetheart. -Yes.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:58.400
He's a national treasure. -Yes.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:01.501
Cooper Hoffman, who plays Gary in "Licorice Pizza."

00:04:01.501 --> 00:04:03.634
-Yeah, he's great. -And -- He's amazing.

00:04:03.634 --> 00:04:06.167
And, you know, we start the scene.

00:04:06.167 --> 00:04:08.667
And to take it even back before --

00:04:08.667 --> 00:04:10.367
Before we shot this movie,

00:04:10.367 --> 00:04:14.968
Paul gathered, you know, all the newcomers on the movie,

00:04:14.968 --> 00:04:16.501
me and Cooper.

00:04:16.501 --> 00:04:19.400
And we watched "American Graffiti."

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:24.567
And there's this infamous story that Toad in the first --

00:04:24.567 --> 00:04:27.033
one of the first scenes is riding this Vespa.

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:28.801
And he crashes and he doesn't break.

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:30.000
He doesn't break character.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.434
He doesn't go like, "Oh, sorry, guys."

00:04:31.434 --> 00:04:34.200
And Paul made it clear like, "You guys can never break.

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:35.801
Like, you've never done this before.

00:04:35.801 --> 00:04:37.601
Just never break."

00:04:37.601 --> 00:04:40.100
And so I take that as, like, gospel.

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:42.467
Like, I'm like, "Oh, the rules of acting.

00:04:42.467 --> 00:04:44.567
Number one, don't break."

00:04:44.567 --> 00:04:45.734
-Wow.

00:04:45.734 --> 00:04:47.801
-Number two, I don't know yet.

00:04:47.801 --> 00:04:49.400
Those were the rules.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:51.300
And so I'm in this truck.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:52.934
It's the time, and I'm so nervous.

00:04:52.934 --> 00:04:55.100
And we start driving. And I don't know what happened.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:56.734
I mean, again, bad driver.

00:04:56.734 --> 00:05:00.133
I must have done something to make a popping noise.

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:01.767
There was just a pop.

00:05:01.767 --> 00:05:03.567
But I didn't think anything of it.

00:05:03.567 --> 00:05:07.067
And then, all of a sudden, from the corner of the cab that we --

00:05:07.067 --> 00:05:11.400
that, you know, in the truck, it started filling with smoke.

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:14.400
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:16.033
-Now, this is not part of the script.

00:05:16.033 --> 00:05:19.334
-Well, I think this is a test.

00:05:19.334 --> 00:05:20.567
-Oh, no, no, no. -This is it.

00:05:20.567 --> 00:05:22.234
-You're like, "I'm not breaking character."

00:05:22.234 --> 00:05:24.067
-I'm not breaking character. -"I know the rules.

00:05:24.067 --> 00:05:25.534
I know the rules. I'm not stopping."

00:05:25.534 --> 00:05:27.767
-I'm like -- I'm not breaking.

00:05:27.767 --> 00:05:29.434
-Oh, my God! -This is a test.

00:05:29.434 --> 00:05:31.000
-Yeah. -So, I'm driving.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:34.167
-Flames. -Smoke filling this cab.

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:36.567
-No, no, no. -And finally Bradley Cooper

00:05:36.567 --> 00:05:39.868
turns to me and goes, "Is that normal?"

00:05:39.868 --> 00:05:42.701
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.701 --> 00:05:46.234
And in my mind, I go, "Acting."

00:05:46.234 --> 00:05:47.934
God.

00:05:47.934 --> 00:05:49.701
[ Laughter ]

00:05:49.701 --> 00:05:52.033
-Incredible. -Incredible.

00:05:52.033 --> 00:05:54.200
-And I go, "This is what they like to call improv."

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:56.167
-Wow. "Is that normal?"

00:05:56.167 --> 00:05:58.133
-"Is that --" Yeah, and I go --

00:05:58.133 --> 00:06:00.901
Okay, so, I've learned in improv --

00:06:00.901 --> 00:06:02.968
Again, number two, improv. Always say "yes."

00:06:02.968 --> 00:06:04.734
-Yes, yes. -'Cause you got to keep --

00:06:04.734 --> 00:06:06.200
So we have two rules now in acting.

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:08.033
-Alana, we're learning a lot from you tonight.

00:06:08.033 --> 00:06:10.601
-So much. You're welcome. -Yeah, yeah. Of course.

00:06:10.601 --> 00:06:12.667
Don't break and -- -Don't break and --

00:06:12.667 --> 00:06:14.400
-Yes and. -Yes and. Of course.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:16.634
So he goes, "Is that normal?"

00:06:16.634 --> 00:06:19.267
And I go..."Yes."

00:06:19.267 --> 00:06:22.133
[ Laughter ]

00:06:22.133 --> 00:06:23.901
-That's your answer? -That's my answer.

00:06:23.901 --> 00:06:25.667
Because that's the rule. No, just "yes."

00:06:25.667 --> 00:06:26.834
-Yes. Okay.

00:06:26.834 --> 00:06:28.400
-And in my mind, I go -- -Nailed it.

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:29.667
-Nailed it.

00:06:29.667 --> 00:06:31.467
[ Laughter ]

00:06:31.467 --> 00:06:32.567
-Nailed it!

00:06:32.567 --> 00:06:34.634
-Nailed it. Just like -- -"Is that normal?"

00:06:34.634 --> 00:06:36.634
"Yes."

00:06:36.634 --> 00:06:39.601
-And we drive for another minute and finally the take is over.

00:06:39.601 --> 00:06:41.033
And I just have been basking.

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:43.334
I'm like, "Wow, God, Alana, you're in the movies now.

00:06:43.334 --> 00:06:46.167
Look at what you just did. That was incredible."

00:06:46.167 --> 00:06:49.300
And I go to turn to my fellow actors in the --

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:51.367
We call them actors.

00:06:51.367 --> 00:06:53.167
My fellow actors. -Of course, yes.

00:06:53.167 --> 00:06:55.234
-And I turn to them thinking, you know --

00:06:55.234 --> 00:06:57.934
I'm gonna say, like, "Wow, guys, what a great time."

00:06:57.934 --> 00:07:00.067
And I turn, and they're gone.

00:07:00.067 --> 00:07:01.567
-They split. They're smart.

00:07:01.567 --> 00:07:03.167
-They're fully gone. -Yeah.

00:07:03.167 --> 00:07:06.133
-And then I hear, "Get out of the truck!"

00:07:06.133 --> 00:07:09.000
I leave. It ended up being something very innocent.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:11.534
It was totally fine. We were going to be totally fine.

00:07:11.534 --> 00:07:14.501
But I didn't break. -That's what I'm talking about.

00:07:14.501 --> 00:07:18.033
That's how you act. That's how you do it.

00:07:18.033 --> 00:07:19.901
[ Applause ]

00:07:19.901 --> 00:07:21.434
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:07:21.434 --> 00:07:24.667
Here's Alana Haim and her real life family in "Licorice Pizza."

00:07:24.667 --> 00:07:26.133
Take a look at this.

00:07:26.133 --> 00:07:28.434
-Why would you do that?! Why would you do that?!

00:07:28.434 --> 00:07:30.200
He was maybe gonna be my boyfriend!

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:31.501
-Listen, young lady.

00:07:31.501 --> 00:07:33.400
You don't bring this idiot to Shabbat dinner here!

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:36.300
-Listen, Dad, he's an atheist and an actor and he's famous!

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:37.834
-But he's Jewish! -He was going to take me

00:07:37.834 --> 00:07:40.133
out of here. Este, don't you even look at me.

00:07:40.133 --> 00:07:42.067
Don't even look at me! You're always looking at me.

00:07:42.067 --> 00:07:43.934
What are you doing?! -I didn't even say anything.

00:07:43.934 --> 00:07:45.667
-What are you doing?! What are you thinking, huh?!

00:07:45.667 --> 00:07:47.367
"I'm Este. I work for Mom and Dad.

00:07:47.367 --> 00:07:49.167
I'm perfect. I'm a real-estate agent.

00:07:49.167 --> 00:07:50.968
Alana doesn't have her life together.

00:07:50.968 --> 00:07:53.400
Alana brings home stupid boyfriends all the time."

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:54.667
-I mean... -I knew it.

00:07:54.667 --> 00:07:56.667
I knew that was what you were thinking.

00:07:56.667 --> 00:07:58.300
You're always thinking things, you thinker.

00:07:58.300 --> 00:08:01.300
You thinker! You think things!

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:04.834
-You thinker! Alana Haim, everybody!

00:08:04.834 --> 00:08:06.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:09.334
"Licorice Pizza" is in select theaters now

00:08:09.334 --> 00:08:12.067
and opens nationwide on Christmas Day.

00:08:12.067 --> 00:08:14.133
Happy, happy birthday, buddy. -Thank you.

